  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on comparing the probabilities of the maximum outcomes and prefers the lottery with the lower probability of the maximum outcome (Lottery A in this case). However, the individual chose Lottery B and justified the choice based on certainty and the small difference in outcomes, not on the probability of the maximum outcome per se. The individual did consider the 33% chance of the maximum in A and the 100% in B, but used this information to support a certainty-based, risk-averse argument rather than applying a rule that favors lower probabilities of maximum outcomes. There is no indication that the individual applied a rule that prefers lower probabilities of maximum outcomes; instead, the reasoning aligns more with expected utility or satisficing based on certainty. Therefore, the decision reason was not used.",
